From 1492f8e0eb18799f3bbd9bb74e9c6b418fa11144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:35:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] Round 1: Add the typed score-matrix API

Add Prepared::score_matrix and MatrixScore in Rust, a GIL-free native
score_matrix in Python with a wrapper that accepts lists or 2-D NumPy
arrays, a CRAFT_MATRIX mode in examples/performance.rs, matrix sides in
validation/performance_pair.py and --matrix in
validation/optimize_performance.py. Batch dispatch and per-candidate
outcome classification are shared with the JSON paths.

Workload: serial (96 candidates, one worker), round 0 lean scores_json
before, round 1 matrix after.
Official 11-sample run: 4.207 ms -> 2.932 ms, 1.43x. The samples are
bimodal because the host speed regime changed during the run.
41-sample confirmation: 3.004 ms -> 2.871 ms, ratio of medians 1.05x,
median per-pair ratio 1.01x. The native gain on this domain-bound
workload is about 1%; the round is kept because it is required.
Supplementary: domain2 2.17x, invalid 46.5x (lean before, matrix after).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
